Changes from the upstream work
------------------------------

This plugin is not the HarnessMM research codebase. It is a DeepSeek Harness
Host plugin that re-implements the Guarded Decision Reuse (GDR) and Certified
Callback Substitution (CCS) contracts for a general-purpose harness. Relative
to upstream:

  * It is derived from the upstream modules
    `integrations/deepseek_harness/sar_v2.mjs` and
    `integrations/deepseek_harness/cot_jev.mjs` (the `ExecutableSubdag`
    controller and the v6 authored-bank contract), not the full repository.
  * The upstream token-based admission rules (slow-token priors, the
    `net > 1024` threshold, TRAIN-partition medians) are omitted. Admission
    is structural instead: a minimum literal chain length plus a public-byte
    cap plus deterministic receipt-guard satisfaction.
  * The upstream fast-selector path, which posts a one-token classification
    request to a loopback-only provider endpoint and accounts response
    logprobs, is omitted. This plugin never makes an extra model call: a
    request is either answered from an already-decided action or it is not.
  * Provider and model pinning (`options.model !== this.model`) is removed,
    because the harness can change models mid-session.
  * The Python research runners, benchmark controllers, recursive
    self-improvement (RSI) loops, configurations and datasets are not
    included and are not required by this plugin.
  * Persistence, session projection and the compaction-time controller message
    rewrite are not implemented; the authored plan stays in the conversation
    as ordinary assistant text.

No HarnessMM benchmark results, measured token savings, or published numbers
are reproduced here or claimed by this plugin.
